Binary ea_iid sha256 22f1319ae347ab4e187953c9161219893310569965234876fdbd6a73daba7349 (unchanged before/after; same as the author's).
HEAD moved 834ffeb -> e415c0e during verification (concurrent commits on the branch); no cpp/ change, binary identical, so the runs are comparable.
Env for every tool run: EA_ALLOW_SHORT_DATASET=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2, 10,000 samples -> NON-COMPLIANT short-dataset runs (brief ground rule 5).

(a) observed.txt shows the claimed defect: 19 of 19 statistics have C0+C1+C2 < 10,000 (sums 10..132 in my first run, 10..97 in the restored run;
    the author's run had 11..116), IID=true rc=0, and "keys that could name the number of permutations evaluated: none".
    Independent check (logs/verify/PROV-23-stop-rule-fingerprint.txt): every partial statistic in the author's p.json and both of mine has
    min(C0+C1, C1+C2) == 6 EXACTLY -- the fingerprint of stopping at the first permutation where both sums exceed 5 (permutation_tests.h:672-674),
    0 violations in 57 statistic rows. The code reading agrees: PermutationTestResult (permutation_test_result.h) has iteration, dataLayout and
    19 doubles, no denominator; grep of cpp/ for permutationsEvaluated|permutationRounds|permCount|iterationsRun|roundsEvaluated: nothing.
(b) control: lag-64 anti-correlated input, permutation battery runs (chi-square and LRS pass) and 8 statistics FAIL; exactly those 8 have
    C0+C1+C2 == 10,000 and min(C0+C1,C1+C2) <= 5 (never satisfied the stop), the 11 passing statistics still stop early (sums 11..1440).
    The control differs from run.sh in the input AND in -q -> -vv; the JSON key sets differ only by hAssessed (pass) vs errorClass/errorMessage
    (fail) -- verbosity does not add or remove any permutation-result key (logs/verify/PROV-23-json-keyset-compare.txt), so the second
    difference is immaterial. The control does NOT show "partial sum" for the statistics that ran to 10,000; it cannot show a denominator key
    because no input can make the binary emit one -- that half of the claim rests on the code reading, not on the control.
(c) run.sh logic: PASS requires partial>0 AND no denominator-like key; an absent/unparseable JSON -> python exception -> res empty -> FAIL (not vacuous);
    an empty permutationTestResults -> partial=0 -> NODEFECT -> FAIL. Weakness noted: byit[i].get(s,0) treats an ABSENT per-iteration key as 0
    (instrument rule 2 shape) -- unreachable with this binary (GetAsJson omits a field only at the -1 sentinel and populateTestCase sets all 19
    from C[][] >= 0), so it cannot have produced this PASS. The denominator search is a token heuristic (evaluated/rounds/total/denominator/
    permutations/permcount/nperm/iterationsrun); its "none" is confirmed by my own full-key walk and the header read above.
    Rule 7 mutation: added token 'layout' -> the nested key dataLayout is found -> "NODEFECT" -> RESULT: FAIL exit 1 (logs/verify/PROV-23-mutation-observed.txt).
    This also proves the walker reaches the nested objects where a real denominator field would sit. run.sh restored by cp from the saved copy;
    sha256 bdb4c404... identical to the before-hash; control.sh untouched (2d3b9df1...). Restored run.sh re-run: RESULT: PASS exit 0.
Provenance: the early termination (c34d4911, Joshua E. Hill, 2018-10-04) and the iteration-indexed PermutationTestResult are UPSTREAM code,
    present verbatim in upstream/master (87c104d) permutation_tests.h:669-670 and permutation_test_result.h:13,38-39; the fork added only dataLayout
    (25fbb54, NOVEL-03). Not documented in README.md, cpp/README.md, NOTICE, FORK-DIVERGENCE-AND-TRUST.md or upstream README; documented only in
    this audit's logs/analysis/iid-permutation.md 2.1 (verdict-equivalence proof, re-derived and found sound) and 2.9.
Verdict: CONFIRMED. Severity LOW, direction neutral: the IID verdict is unchanged (proof in 2.1 holds: both sums are non-decreasing, so a statistic
